The synthetic benchmark generator (tabular_xai.engine.synthetic) produces
data whose structure is inspired by common Kaggle-style tabular
competitions: nonlinear feature interactions, a redundant collinear
proxy feature, and a subtly leaky post-outcome sensor feature.

This product depends on third-party open-source libraries (LightGBM,
PyTorch, scikit-learn, SHAP, pandas, Plotly, FastMCP among others),
each under its own license.
